Found the bug. On line 571-578 of `setup.go`, the pre-selection logic on re-run adds **both** installed agents AND detected agents:

```go
// Build pre-selection set: installed agents (always) + detected agents
for _, name := range installedAgentNames {
    preSelectedSet[name] = struct{}{}
}
for _, ag := range detected {
    preSelectedSet[ag.Name()] = struct{}{}
}
```

After deselecting Gemini CLI, its hooks are removed, but the `.gemini/` directory still exists. So `DetectAll()` still detects it, and it gets pre-selected again.

The fix: on re-run, only pre-select agents that have hooks installed. Detected-but-not-installed agents should still appear as options, just not pre-selected.

